{"actions":[{"action":"success_contract","content":{"objective":"Start /app/alpine.iso in QEMU in the background so that telnet 127.0.0.1 6665 connects to the VM console and shows a login prompt, then leave it running and block until it is ready.","required_artifacts":["A running QEMU process booting /app/alpine.iso","A reachable telnet service on 127.0.0.1:6665 connected to the VM console"],"required_behaviors":["QEMU must be started in the background","Port 6665 on localhost must accept telnet connections","Connecting via telnet must present a login prompt","The VM must remain running after readiness is confirmed"],"known_invalid_patterns":["File existence or ISO presence without a running VM","QEMU started without telnet/serial forwarding to 127.0.0.1:6665","Smoke checks that do not demonstrate the login prompt","Stopping the VM after boot instead of leaving it running"],"verification_plan":["Inspect available tools and environment for qemu/telnet support","Launch QEMU with console forwarded to tcp:127.0.0.1:6665 and background it","Probe readiness by connecting to 127.0.0.1:6665 and confirming the login prompt appears","Keep the process running and report receipt-backed evidence"],"finalization_evidence_required":["Receipt showing the QEMU launch command and background PID","Receipt showing successful connection to 127.0.0.1:6665","Receipt showing the login prompt from the VM console"],"notes":["Prerequisites like tool availability are not success by themselves; they only inform implementation."]}},{"action":"plan_update","content":{"objective":"Start /app/alpine.iso in QEMU in the background so telnet 127.0.0.1 6665 reaches the VM console and shows a login prompt, then leave it running.","current_focus":"Discover available tooling and launch parameters, then boot the ISO with console forwarding to localhost:6665.","implementation_approach":["Inspect environment for qemu/telnet or equivalent tools.","Use raw_bash to launch QEMU in background with serial/monitor forwarded appropriately.","Use probe_service or a direct telnet-style connection check to confirm readiness.","Preserve the running process after readiness is confirmed."],"validation_strategy":["Confirm the port is listening and reachable on 127.0.0.1:6665.","Confirm the telnet session displays a login prompt from the guest.","Retain receipts for launch and readiness checks."],"verification_test_strategy":["If probe_service is available, measure service readiness on 127.0.0.1:6665.","Otherwise use raw_bash with a short scripted telnet/nc connection to capture the prompt.","Avoid relying on ISO existence or process start alone."],"known_bad_behavior":["Launching QEMU without console forwarding to the requested port.","Treating boot start as success before the login prompt is observed.","Killing the VM after verification."],"evidence_gaps":["No evidence yet of tool availability or a running VM.","No receipt-backed proof of telnet reachability or login prompt."],"risks":["QEMU may not be installed or may require alternate flags.","The ISO may boot slowly, requiring polling until ready."],"next_steps":["Inspect tools and filesystem for qemu/telnet support and the ISO path.","Launch the VM in background.","Poll readiness until the login prompt is observed."],"finalization_evidence_required":["Launch receipt with PID","Readiness receipt showing 127.0.0.1:6665 reachable","Receipt showing login prompt"],"notes":["Do not finalize on prerequisites alone."]}}]}
